Actually, without adding a new field, we can simplify this: in the 10th frame, `g.tenthFrameRolls = g.frameRolls` is redundant — frameRolls is already tracking that. Let's simplify: use frameRolls directly in the 10th frame, and add a strike check. In the 10th frame, the game ends after the 2nd roll only if the first roll was not a strike. The first roll was a strike only if pins == 10 on the first roll. We can check `g.rolls[len(g.rolls)-2] == 10` (the first roll of the 10th frame). More simply: when frameRolls == 2, check whether the first roll of the frame was 10.

